From 17cc2f03f149f3b8c8d4c007b4d85a9941e619b4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Calogero Mandracchia <calogero@efebia.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 19:47:40 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] rmcp-client: observe connections and hold stdio
 relaunches

Number a client's connections as their initialize responses arrive, and
tag each subscribed custom notification with the connection that read it.
Add the client's current experimental capabilities to every initialize,
those of recovered connections included, and count notifications dropped
by full subscriber queues.

Expose the connection's phase, generation and process ID, with a revision
that changes on every transition, including the exit of a connection that
is not recovered. While launches are held, recovery starts no replacement
and stops one that is still initializing; held time spends none of the
restart budget.
